cms/

# ── Nothing below this line may leave this machine ──────────────────────────
#
# The Vercel CLI reads THIS file and its own defaults. It does not read
# .gitignore — so a file being untracked says nothing about whether
# `vercel deploy` would upload it. Its defaults exclude .env.local and not .env.
#
# Every deployment of this project so far has been git-based (94 of 94 checked
# via the deployments API: zero without a commit sha), so nothing here has ever
# been uploaded. This list is what keeps that true the first time someone runs
# a deploy from the folder instead of pushing.
#
# Secrets and the legacy order backup — which held real customer names and
# addresses — now live outside the project entirely, in a sibling directory.
# .env stays because the local production build reads it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.rebuild-secrets.json
.sanity-*
.simshots*
.devdb/
*.pem
*.key
